  "status_text": "Twelve cards can cover all 16,777,216 ways to set twenty-four switches. Make eight groups of three. Each card crosses out one of the eight possible settings in each group. Set the switches however you like. At least one card crosses out none of the settings in front of you. That deck also gives twelve candidates for spotting which groups are all on. Each makes a quadratic guess using only the three switches in each group. For every setting, one candidate gets all eight answers right. Lean checked both steps (L-lib-599, L-lib-585).",
